PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key criteria from NI 45-106 (Jan 2021): individual income test (>200k solo or >300k joint spouse, each of prior 2 yrs + expectation); net fin assets (>1M solo/with spouse); net assets (>5M solo/with spouse); entity qualifies if net assets >=5M on statements OR all equity owners themselves AIs.

B actually qualifies (joint spousal income 320k/350k exceeds 300k threshold; multiple colleagues erred by claiming aggregation disallowed). C meets exact 5M net-assets test. D meets entity net-assets (>=10M cash from Jose). A meets "all owners AIs" (LPs + GP holding co with 6M assets). E fails both entity tests: Alex/Bob are not AIs, and net assets cannot be confirmed (>=5M) because investment-property values unspecified (only 5.5M GIC - 0.3M known liab = 5.2M, insufficient).

Disagreements center on misapplications of spousal-income aggregation and entity look-through rules. E is only option that does not qualify on facts.}

